+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+See proposal.md and specs/product-reviews/spec.md. The shop layer exposes product review DTOs through separate public and private endpoints, while review persistence and product persistence are handled by the core services. Existing review DTO inheritance currently risks serializing customer details, and product rating fields are not consistently recalculated across the review lifecycle.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+
+- Enforce review input and ownership rules before persistence.
+- Make the public representation an explicit privacy-safe projection.
+- Centralize review lookup by product and aggregate recalculation so create, update, and delete share the same behavior.
+- Preserve merchant endpoint compatibility while returning the specified HTTP errors.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+
+- Changing customer-review functionality unrelated to product reviews.
+- Adding moderation, voting, pagination, or new review storage tables.
+- Reworking authentication; use the existing authenticated customer context.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Use a dedicated public review response shape/populator rather than exposing the persistence/entity inheritance graph. This prevents accidental email/address leakage and makes the allowlist stable; serializer annotations alone would leave future entity fields risky.
+- Validate rating at the API boundary and again in the service/facade before writing. The boundary provides a clean 400 response, while the service guard protects other callers and prevents invalid data from reaching persistence.
+- Check customer/product uniqueness before create and map the conflict to 409. Keep the check in the transactional service path so rejected requests do not create partial records.
+- Resolve merchant reviews with a product-constrained lookup, mapping null to the existing not-found exception. This treats a review attached to another product the same as a missing review.
+- Recalculate aggregates from the authoritative review set after each mutation, using `BigDecimal` with one-decimal `HALF_UP` rounding and explicit zero values for an empty set. Recalculation is preferred over incremental deltas because it remains correct after edits and deletes.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Concurrent duplicate submissions] → Enforce uniqueness transactionally where supported and retain the service check; add coverage for the normal duplicate path.
+- [Existing clients expect inherited customer fields] → The public endpoint intentionally narrows its contract for privacy; merchant/private responses remain separate.
+- [Legacy inconsistent product aggregates] → Recalculate on every lifecycle mutation; existing stale products may require a one-time data repair outside this ticket.
+
+## Migration Plan
+
+Deploy the shop/core changes and tests together. No schema migration is required. Roll back the application deployment if endpoint behavior causes an issue; persisted reviews remain compatible with the existing model.
