+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Product reviews currently expose customer data through the public response and accept invalid or unauthorized submissions. Review lifecycle operations also leave product rating aggregates stale, making the storefront inaccurate after edits and deletions.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Restrict public product-review JSON to review id, rating, description, date, and reviewer first name.
+- Enforce whole-number ratings from 1 through 5, one review per customer/product, and ownership of the submitted customer id with 400, 409, and 403 responses respectively.
+- Add reliable merchant update and delete behavior with 404 responses for missing or mismatched reviews.
+- Recalculate product rating and ratingCount after review creation, update, and deletion, using one-decimal half-up rounding and zero values when no reviews remain.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `product-reviews`: Public review privacy, customer submission rules, merchant lifecycle operations, and product rating aggregation.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- No existing specifications are present in this repository. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected modules include the shop REST controllers, facades, populators and DTOs, core review repositories/services, product persistence and rating aggregation, exception-to-HTTP handling, and integration/unit tests for review and product endpoints.
